WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:03.639
On paper, Solo: A Star Wars Story wasn't the
worst idea.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:06.059
But in practice, the project didn't really
work out.

00:00:06.369 --> 00:00:12.539
The Han Solo Star Wars prequel was released
in May 2018 to a less-than-enthusiastic reception,

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:15.839
becoming one of the worst-performing movies
in the entire series.

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:20.079
Far from the billion dollar heights of The
Force Awakens, Solo brought in only about

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:26.149
$393 million at the global box office a shockingly
low sum for what used to be the biggest movie

00:00:26.149 --> 00:00:27.179
franchise in the world.

00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:32.319
Prior to the launch of Solo, it was reported
that Disney was working on other spinoffs

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:36.889
focusing on different characters from the
franchise, including Obi-Wan Kenobi and Boba

00:00:36.889 --> 00:00:37.379
Fett.

00:00:37.459 --> 00:00:42.499
The Boba Fett movie was even reported as having
a writer-director attached in James Mangold,

00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:45.919
who previously helmed the well-received Logan
in 2017.

00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:51.079
But after Solo crashed and burned, those plans
seem to have changed, and at this point, we'd

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:53.099
be surprised if they ever went back to it.

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:58.179
If audiences cared so little about Solo, it's
hard to imagine them getting excited for Boba

00:00:58.179 --> 00:00:58.679
Fett.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:03.899
Imagine a movie that combined cowboys, ninjas,
and Vikings, starring Chris Pratt in the lead

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:05.779
role as the cowboy-ninja-viking.

00:01:05.779 --> 00:01:07.129
Sounds fun enough, right?

00:01:07.129 --> 00:01:08.979
Well, it wasn't meant to be.

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:14.439
Based on a 2009 limited series from Image
Comics, Cowboy Ninja Viking was announced

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:20.989
by Universal Pictures in 2017, and then delayed
indefinitely in August 2018, only a month

00:01:20.989 --> 00:01:22.859
before production had been set to start.

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:27.759
Pratt was slated to play the main character
Duncan, a super-soldier with a personality

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:31.239
disorder, splitting his identity into three
distinct power sets.

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:36.979
It was originally set for release in June
2019 with a budget of around $65 million,

00:01:36.989 --> 00:01:40.989
but was reportedly plagued by script issues
which helped lead to its collapse.

00:01:40.989 --> 00:01:45.099
According to The Hollywood Reporter, rumors
of the film's impending shutdown flew around

00:01:45.099 --> 00:01:49.329
Hollywood for months, meaning it wasn't too
much of a surprise that the movie didn't come

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:51.999
together even if it is disappointing for fans
of the comic.

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:58.599
Supernatural goth comic adaptation The Crow
hit theaters in 1994, and it feels like Hollywood

00:01:58.599 --> 00:02:00.839
has been trying to remake the movie ever since.

00:02:00.839 --> 00:02:04.239
But every time it starts to come together,
the project hits a wall.

00:02:04.419 --> 00:02:08.739
A revolving door of actors have been attached
or been rumored to be attached to the role

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:13.319
of undead avenger Eric Draven, which was first
made popular by Brandon Lee.

00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:18.489
The list includes Tom Hiddleston, Alexander
Skarsgard, Luke Evans, Jack Huston and more

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:22.908
and that's not even getting into all of the
potential directors who have come and gone.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:27.459
Production was finally set to begin in 2015
before the bankruptcy of production company

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:29.879
Relativity Media shut the project down.

00:02:30.139 --> 00:02:35.309
By late 2016, financing had reportedly been
secured for another attempt with Jason Momoa

00:02:35.309 --> 00:02:38.779
in the lead role and The Nun's Corin Hardy
in the director's chair.

00:02:39.029 --> 00:02:43.739
In March 2018, Variety reported that Sony
was setting a release date for The Crow for

00:02:43.749 --> 00:02:49.539
October 2019 but just over two months later,
Deadline broke the news that Momoa and Hardy

00:02:49.539 --> 00:02:50.279
had moved on.

00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:53.599
Not long after that, Sony took the movie off
its schedule.

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:59.239
Neil Blomkamp made a huge impression in 2009
with his debut feature, the sci-fi parable

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:00.239
District 9.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:04.849
While he's since produced two more full-length
movies with Elysium and Chappie, he also makes

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:07.179
short films with his company Oats Studio.

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:12.999
In 2017, the company made a 27-minute short
called "Firebase," set during the Vietnam

00:03:12.999 --> 00:03:17.859
War and focusing on some American soldiers
who experience some very freaky occurrences.

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:21.039
"They were monsters… in the shape of men.”

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:24.519
"And they wouldn't die."

00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:28.659
After the short was released online, it was
announced that the studio planned to adapt

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:32.479
it into a full-length feature, if a crowdfunding
drive was successful enough.

00:03:32.799 --> 00:03:34.599
Long story short, it wasn't.

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:39.759
In April 2018, Oats Studios tweeted the news
that the longer version of "Firebase" was

00:03:39.759 --> 00:03:42.819
dead, and that all contributors would have
their money refunded.

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:47.139
As they wrote in their since-deleted message,
"Unfortunately we didn't raise enough to do

00:03:47.139 --> 00:03:48.519
something truly awesome.

00:03:48.779 --> 00:03:51.709
We would rather over-deliver than create an
average film.

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:54.099
We thank the thousands of people who did back
us."

